\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Two held-out readings of the rule-constrained arm on CartPole-v1, one per column group. ``Hybrid'' is what the arm reports: the composed system, bank included. ``Network only'' re-evaluates each constrained arm's saved checkpoint with the rule substitution disabled, so it is the learned policy's own return. ``Unconstrained'' is the baseline actor on the same reset seeds. The two readings answer different questions and are not alternatives to one another. A positive substitution gain means the frozen rule bank scored better than the network it was induced from.}}{15}{table.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:attribution}{{3}{15}{Two held-out readings of the rule-constrained arm on CartPole-v1, one per column group. ``Hybrid'' is what the arm reports: the composed system, bank included. ``Network only'' re-evaluates each constrained arm's saved checkpoint with the rule substitution disabled, so it is the learned policy's own return. ``Unconstrained'' is the baseline actor on the same reset seeds. The two readings answer different questions and are not alternatives to one another. A positive substitution gain means the frozen rule bank scored better than the network it was induced from}{table.caption.10}{}}
