\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Mechanism of the training-time constraint, as implemented. The top row is the hypothesis that the threshold-relaxation experiment refutes. The bottom row is the loop the code implements: a hard one-hot mask, whose log-probability at a masked step is exactly zero and which therefore contributes nothing to the policy gradient, together with a rule bank re-induced from the masked trajectory every $50$ episodes, which makes the mask's own output the evidence for its own rules.}}{17}{figure.caption.12}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:constraint-mechanism}{{4}{17}{Mechanism of the training-time constraint, as implemented. The top row is the hypothesis that the threshold-relaxation experiment refutes. The bottom row is the loop the code implements: a hard one-hot mask, whose log-probability at a masked step is exactly zero and which therefore contributes nothing to the policy gradient, together with a rule bank re-induced from the masked trajectory every $50$ episodes, which makes the mask's own output the evidence for its own rules}{figure.caption.12}{}}
